<v Adam Ray>(SINGING) A lot of my friends-- they have kids. Ooh, good for you. Ohhh, good for you. Who cares? Who cares? Who cares? Who cares?
<v Adam Ray>（歌唱）我很多朋友……他们有孩子了。噢，那真是太好了。噢，那真是太好了。谁在乎呢？谁在乎呢？

00:23:20.370 --> 00:23:39.720
<v Chris Benderev>But then the song shifts. Adam Ray says-- or sings-- that he and his wife are still deciding about having kids. And suddenly, he turns to the crowd, wants to find someone with kids who can make an argument for having them. Adam starts in the front row, with the guy a few seats away from Stacey and Michael.
<v Chris Benderev>但随后歌曲变调了。亚当·雷说——或者唱着——他和妻子还在考虑要不要孩子。突然，他转向人群，想找一个有孩子的人来为生孩子辩护。亚当从前排开始，找到了坐在离斯泰西和迈克尔几个座位远的一个男人。

00:23:39.720 --> 00:23:41.350
<v Adam Ray>(SINGING) Do you have kids?
<v Adam Ray>（歌唱）你有孩子吗？

